(PR Summary: Reduce Agentic Codexa Overhead) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Project: codexa) Tj T*
(- Branch: codex/general/codexa-20260718-000156-focus-orientation) Tj T*
(- Base: main) Tj T*
(- Source head before final summary refresh: e05804a50f79) Tj T*
(- Subject: perf\(mcp\): reduce agentic Codexa overhead) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Goal and Outcome) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(This change targets the archived agent A/B failure in which the Codexa-enabled) Tj T*
(arm used 5.94x the control's input tokens while producing the same verified) Tj T*
(completion result. The current candidate removes the mandatory lifecycle call) Tj T*
(chain, defaults agent hosts to a three-tool MCP surface, and tells agents to use) Tj T*
(zero Codexa calls for exact local tasks.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(An authenticated one-pair regression smoke on the same checked-in task did not) Tj T*
(reproduce the 5.94x failure:) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(| Actual model usage | Control | Current Codexa treatment | Ratio |) Tj T*
(| --- | ---: | ---: | ---: |) Tj T*
(| Input tokens | 108,683 | 127,190 | 1.17x |) Tj T*
(| Cached input tokens | 76,032 | 109,568 | 1.44x |) Tj T*
(| Output tokens | 3,065 | 3,551 | 1.16x |) Tj T*
(| Codexa tool calls | 0 | 0 | no difference |) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(The treatment used the intended zero-call route, passed the public tests, and) Tj T*
(passed all committed hidden behavior cases plus 40 generated cases. The single) Tj T*
(control run passed its public tests but failed the leading/trailing C1 control) Tj T*
(case. This is a non-confirmatory one-pair smoke, not a broad product-effect) Tj T*
(estimate. It has no task-clustered interval or comparable provider-cost metric.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(What Changed) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Smaller default agent surface) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Agent launchers now default to the core MCP profile: search, changeplan,) Tj T*
(and capabilities.) Tj T*
(- capabilities retains access to all 22 logical operations, while the full) Tj T*
(direct-tool profile remains an explicit opt-in.) Tj T*
(- Server instructions and tool guidance make raw source reads terminal when an) Tj T*
(exact target is already known.) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(Selective lifecycle cadence) Tj T*
() Tj T*
(- Exact file, symbol, command, config, and quoted-error work can use zero Codexa) Tj T*
(calls.) Tj T*
(- A normal bounded change usually uses at most two calls; only an ambiguous,) Tj T*
(materially risky change without a managed completion gate uses the narrow) Tj T*
(three-call exception.) Tj T*
(- Managed hooks coalesce duplicate work and retain an evidence-bearing final) Tj T*
(review only when the host can provide meaningful verification evidence.) Tj T*
ET
